'''Manuel Alejandro Cota Cárdenas''' (born 26 December 1991) is a Mexican politician from the [[Ecologist Green Party of Mexico]] (PVEM). Born in [[La Paz, Baja California Sur]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.imagenradio.com.mx/noticias/quien-es-manuel-alejandro-cota-cardenas-nuevo-coordinador-4t-baja-california-sur|title=¿Quién es Manuel Alejandro Cota Cárdenas, nuevo coordinador de la 4T en Baja California Sur?|language=Es|first=Ricardo|last=Lara|date=29 September 2026|website=[[Imagen Radio]]|access-date=29 September 2026}}</ref> he is the son of [[Leonel Cota Montaño]], [[governor of Baja California Sur]] between 1999 and 2005.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.diarioelindependiente.mx/2021/05/los-necesitamos-monreal-llama-a-leonel-cota-a-respaldar-a-victor-castro|title='Lo necesitamos': Monreal llama a Leonel Cota a respaldar a Víctor Castro|first=Rodrigo|last=Rebolledo Ramírez|date=17 May 2021|newspaper=Diario El Independiente|language=es|access-date=29 September 2026}}</ref>

He was elected to the [[Chamber of Deputies (Mexico)|Chamber of Deputies]] for [[1st federal electoral district of Baja California Sur|Baja California Sur's 1st district]] in the [[2024 Mexican general election|2024 general election]], receiving 56% of the votes cast in a three-way race.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.sdpnoticias.com/estados/baja-california-sur/quien-es-manuel-cota-diputado-del-partido-verde-por-baja-california-sur/|title=¿Quién es Manuel Cota? Diputado del Partido Verde por Baja California Sur|language=Es|website=SDP Noticias|first=Eduardo|last=Mendoza|date=30 October 2025|access-date=29 September 2026}}</ref><ref name=sil66>{{cite web |title=Perfil: Dip. Manuel Alejandro Cota Cárdenas, LXVI Legislatura |publisher=[[Secretariat of the Interior|SEGOB]] |website=Sistema de Información Legislativa (SIL) |accessdate=3 September 2024 |url= http://sil.gobernacion.gob.mx/Librerias/pp_PerfilLegislador.php?SID=&Referencia=9228150 |language=es}}</ref><ref name=computos2024>{{cite web |title=Diputaciones: Baja California Sur. Distrito 1. La Paz |url= https://computos2024.ine.mx/diputaciones/nacional/circunscripcion/0/entidad/3/distrito/1/candidatura |website=Cómputos Distritales 2024 |publisher=[[Instituto Nacional Electoral|INE]] |access-date=22 June 2024 |language=es}}</ref> Originally elected for the [[National Regeneration Movement]] (Morena), he switched allegiance to the PVEM at the start of the congressional session.<ref name="mvsnoticias.com">{{Cite web |date=2 September 2024 |title=Arranca apenas la Legislatura y cinco diputados federales piden licencia |url=https://mvsnoticias.com/nacional/2024/9/2/arranca-apenas-la-legislatura-cinco-diputados-federales-piden-licencia-654862.html |access-date=4 September 2024 |website=MVS Noticias |language=es}}</ref><ref name=sil66/>

In 2026, [[Morena (political party)|Morena]], the PVEM's [[Sigamos Haciendo Historia|ally]], announced him as the "state coordinator for the defense of the transformation and national sovereignty", a position expected to represent the party in the [[2027 Mexican local elections|Baja California Sur gubernatorial election]] of 6 June 2027.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://latinus.us/mexico/2026/9/28/morena-apuesta-por-el-apellido-cota-para-baja-california-sur-va-hijo-del-exgobernador-diputado-del-verde-185609.html|title=Morena apuesta por el apellido Cota para Baja California Sur: va hijo del exgobernador y diputado del Verde|language=Es|website=[[Latinus (news portal)|Latinus]]|first=Mauricio|last=Rubí|date=28 September 2026|access-date=29 September 2026}}</ref>

